            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for to jump, then the Urdu for to slip."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: رنگنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رنگنا — rangnā — \"to dye, to colour\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رنگنا (rangnā) is the verb of rang, \"colour\". rang has two possible sources, Sanskrit raṅga, \"dye, colour\" (CDIAL 10560), and Persian rang, \"colour\", and the two may have merged. CDIAL lists a Hindi rãgānā, \"to be coloured\", under raṅgayati, \"dyes\" (CDIAL 10570)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
