        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The phrase, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دستخط کرنا (dastkhat karnā) is \"to do the hand-writing\". dastkhat, \"a signature\", joins Persian dast, \"hand\", and Arabic khaṭṭ, \"a line, writing\" (Lane, root kh-ṭ-ṭ), put together in Persian. karnā comes from Sanskrit karoti, \"does\" (CDIAL 2814)."
            }
          ]
        },
